  "system": {
    "description": "<p>You drape a shroud of void-aspected aether over a creature, making it much more difficult for them to use magic.</p><p>Choose a target within <strong>10 spaces</strong>. Until the start of your next turn, that creature increases the <strong>Complexity</strong> of any casting checks it makes by <strong>+1</strong>.</p><p>Additionally, the <strong>Complexity</strong> of any checks made to counteract the target's spells decrease by <strong>-1</strong> to a minimum of <strong>1</strong>.</p><p>Each extra success extends the duration by <strong>+1 rounds</strong>.</p><p>Alternatively, you may both increase the <strong>Complexity</strong> of the target's casting checks and decrease the complexity of counteract checks made against the target by <strong>+1</strong> per 2 extra successes.</p><p>Magical creatures affected by this spell take <strong>Damage</strong> equal to the complexity modifier at the start of their turn.</p><p><strong>Effect:</strong> @UUID[Compendium.titan-vttrpg-compendium.effects.ActiveEffect.pfJLzNDoqk5EDZTq]{Antimagic Curse}</p>",
